            <ArticleTitle>A Cu(ii)-MOF capable of fixing CO2 from air and showing high capacity H2 and CO2 adsorption.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13371-13374</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc08315g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A porous Cu(ii)-MOF shows an adsorption of 6.6 wt% of H2 at 77 K and 62 bar and a very high 60 wt% of CO2 at 298 K and 32 bar. When air is bubbled into a suspension of the activated MOF in the presence of different epoxides at room temperature, the CO2 in air is readily converted into the corresponding cyclic carbonates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
